  "id": "object-choice",
  "term": "object choice",
  "definition": "Object choice is a learning task in which a subject chooses between objects or locations to find a hidden reward, often using another individual’s cue such as pointing. In this packet, it refers to the standard task used to test whether dogs can use human communicative signals to locate the reward.",
